  "id": "COMPOUND:42873 - PROTEIN:5858",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a mechanistic link between 3-(3,4-Dihydroxy-2-methoxyphenyl)-7-hydroxychromen-4-one and KB, primarily through its interaction with Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9. This compound is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including (2E,4E)-N-isobutylundeca-2,4-dien-8,10-diynamide and (1R,2S,6R,7R,10S,11R,12R,14S)-10,11-dihydroxy-2,6-dimethyl-12-propan-2-yl-13-oxatetracyclo[8.5.0.02,7.012,14]pentadecane-6-carboxylic acid, all of which are linked to KB. The presence of multiple targets in the SDR family, which is involved in metabolic processes and detoxification, supports a role for this compound in modulating these pathways. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism involving the SDR family, but the exact functional role remains unclear. The compound's interaction with SDR family members may influence KB's biological activity, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm this.",
